{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You blew with Your wind, etc.</b> Three punishments corresponding to three thoughts — corresponding to what he said ״אֲחַלֵּק שָׁלָל״ — for the sea swallowed them: even if a horse would carry him and swim through the sea, behold his spoil was lost. And corresponding to the affliction he plotted against the Jews, as alluded to in his saying ״תִּמְלָאֵמוֹ נַפְשִׁי״, and also what he plotted to draw his sword — of this He said <b>they sank</b>, etc., meaning they died; and they did not die immediately and at once, but ״they sank like lead in mighty waters.״ And they said, their memory for blessing (Mekhilta), that the waters would raise them up to the heavens and bring them down to the abyss, and they would die over a prolonged time. And His saying <b>like lead in mighty waters</b> alludes to two things: the first is the sinking, and that is His saying ״they sank like lead״; and the second is the preventing them from dying immediately and at once, and that is His saying ״in mighty waters״ — and they would lift them from above and prevent them from dying immediately and at once. Song and praise to Elohim for His miracles and wonders."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:27.216998377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}